I: RESOLVE BASE PATH BINDING
Locked the base path during bridge initialization instead of injecting it dynamically at runtime.
Result: deterministic, working-directory-independent file resolution.

II: REFACTOR CONFIGURATION & SESSION SERVICE
Moved configuration persistence/validation from KeyboardService into SessionService.
Decoupled KeyboardService from file IO and began its transition toward CommandRouter.
Updated GameEngine bootstrap to use SessionService for configuration lifecycle.

III: EXTRACT BASE ENGINE & EXCEPTION ABSTRACTION
Extracted lifecycle execution, abstract hooks, exit signaling, and exception policy into a generic Engine base class.
Result: GameEngine became declarative, with runtime orchestration and exception boundaries centralized in the base infrastructure.

IV: STANDARDIZE RENDER PIPELINES
Unified rendering and prompt compilation through stateless OutputAssemblyService.hydrate(template, repl_map).
Moved flow orchestration/template ownership into GameEngine and replaced dynamic builders/tag assembly with get_repl_map(prompt_config).
Result: a single declarative template-hydration pipeline with reduced builder overhead.

V: YAML + BOOT / RENDER PIPELINE STANDARDIZATION
Established raw YAML → hydrated App Data Tree flow using strict Pydantic models.
Added dynamic BootService for config ingestion, type resolution, list hydration, and zip_add.
Consolidated keyboard lifecycle under SessionService and removed legacy KeyboardService/SymbolSet dependencies.

VI: MULTI-DOCUMENT FRAGMENT RETRIEVAL & INTERNAL CONFIG
Added MULTI_DOC resolution with aggregated fragment placeholders (§base_fragments§, §domain_fragments§, §prompt_fragments§).
Migrated domain/prompt rendering to the multi-document schema.
Embedded CLANK_CONFIG as the development/runtime configuration source, eliminating duplicate external config.

VII: FLATTENED ASSET RETRIEVAL
Changed MULTI_DOC lookup to build a filename→path map across the entire assets tree.
Result: assets can be reorganized into subfolders without resolver configuration changes.

VIII: SCRIPT-DEV DOMAIN PROMPT ORGANIZATION
Split the monolithic script-dev render into explicit bl-add, bl-impl, and bl-drain flows.
Each flow now resolves only the fragments relevant to its operation, with drain additionally including history.

IX: REMOVAL OF PLAN ABSTRACTION & TEMPLATE OPTIMIZATION
Completely excised legacy 'plan' references from runtime, configuration, and prompt construction pipelines.
Streamlined PROMPT_TEMPLATE down to core multi-document and repo-content placeholders to reduce token overhead.

X: NORMALIZE RUAMEL INSTANCES
Consolidated YAML parsing/dumping across the application to utilize a single shared ruamel.yaml instance.
Result: Eliminated redundant parser instantiation and standardized YAML processing behavior across services.

XI: MAKE TEMPLATES SCRIPT INTERNAL
Refactored AssemblyService to resolve templates directly from built-in memory mappings instead of checking disk assets. Updated Render model defaults to fallback to prompt_template and configured UI renders to explicitly disable base/domain resolution. Removed explicit template references across domain YAML definitions.
Result: Eliminated runtime disk resolution overhead for templates and standardized internal template lookups.

XII: ADD TAIL TRUNCATION TO MULTI-DOCUMENT-RETRIEVAL (MDR)
Updated AssemblyService._resolve() to support both string filenames and objects containing `file` and `tail_lines` keys. Added conditional line slicing logic to prepend `**truncated**\n` when document line count exceeds `tail_lines`. Updated `CLANK_DOMAINS` for `bl-drain` render to apply `{ file: "history-doc.md", tail_lines: 8 }`.
Result: Resolved multi-document retrieval files can now be safely bounded by tail line counts without blowing up prompt size.

XIII: DISPLAY MSG FROM LAST ACTION & UI TEMPLATE UPDATE
Updated UI_TEMPL to feature a top border status bar slot (`§ msg §`). Refactored GameEngine._compile_to_clipboard() to include character counts alongside line counts in ActionResult. Updated GameEngine._render() to inject formatted message string into the UI replacement map prior to hydration.
Result: Last action status messages and prompt metrics are now dynamically displayed inside the TUI header.

XIV: REFACTOR MULTI-DOCUMENT RETRIEVAL TO RESOLVE FROM REPO ROOT
Updated `AssemblyService._resolve()` MULTI_DOC block to expand paths across the repository using `self.files.expand_paths(["."])`. Built an `asset_map` lookup table keyed by file basenames (`path.name`), allowing multi-doc resolvers to locate referenced files across subdirectories without requiring explicit relative paths.
Result: Multi-document retrieval now dynamically resolves file references relative to the project root directory.

XV: RELOCATE YAML CONFIGURATIONS TO DISK ASSETS
Migrated hardcoded configuration strings and domain definitions out of the main script and onto disk within the `.clanker/shared-assets/config-fragments/` directory as individual YAML files. Updated configuration assembly logic to dynamically load and merge `kb_def.yaml` from script resources and `config.yaml` from the workspace root into a unified runtime config, introducing the `ConfigAssemblyFailure` exception type for missing or invalid fragment states.
    - Relocated configuration definitions to disk storage under `.clanker/`
    - Unified configuration loading flow across Clanker and external projects

XVI: STREAMLINE PUD INITIALIZATION & DOCUMENTATION SEEDING
Updated workspace initialization routines to scaffold `.clanker/progress-documentation` and `.clanker/prompt-fragments` subdirectories automatically. Implemented template seeding logic to discover documentation templates with the `.template` extension relative to script assets and populate new progress documentation files using the `.cdoc` extension.
    - Added directory scaffolding for progress tracking and prompt fragments
    - Seeded project workspace with default `.cdoc` documentation templates

XVII: IMPLEMENT DUAL-SOURCE ASSET DISCOVERY (PREPARATORY MIGRATION)
    - Split 'FileBridge.base_path' into 'FileBridge.clanker_path' and 'FileBridge.pud_path' members
    - Updated 'FileBridge.__init__' to correctly assign values to both path attributes
    - Refactored path expansion into distinct 'FileBridge.get_clanker_files' and 'FileBridge.get_pud_files' methods
    - Divided file content reading into dedicated 'FileBridge.read_clanker_asset' and 'FileBridge.read_pud_asset' utilities
    - Migrated 'AssemblyService._resolve' to adopt PUD-specific asset retrieval calls as a foundation for upcoming collision handling

XVIII: DUAL-SOURCE ASSET DISCOVERY IMPLEMENTATION
    - Declared 'IllegalDuplicateFile' exception to handle filename collisions during asset discovery
    - Implemented 'FileBridge.getAssetMap' to scan and merge files from both Clanker and PUD repositories while ignoring '.git' directories
    - Implemented 'FileBridge.getFileContent' to retrieve text content from discovered asset paths
    - Migrated 'AssemblyService._resolve' to rely on dual-source asset mapping for multi-document resolution

XIX: PUD WORKSPACE INITIALIZATION TEMPLATE RELOCATION
    - Updated `initialize_workspace` to source the default configuration template from `.clanker/shared-assets/templates/config.template`
    - Renamed the initialized configuration file to `config.yaml` within the PUD workspace directory

XX: SHARED DOMAINS AND NAMED INCLUDE/EXCLUDE CONFIGURATION SETS
    - Implemented loading and prepending of shared domains from shared assets to ensure fixed-key consistency across repositories
    - Added parsing and storage of top-level named include/exclude sets (`sets` block) in configuration data
    - Introduced pre-validation recursive traversal (`_resolve_sets`) to detect and substitute reference pointers (`varname` or `set`) with literal `includes` and `excludes` values

XXI: MULTI_DOC ASSET COLLISION RESOLUTION AND FULL-PATH FILE RETRIEVAL
    - Resolved a critical bug where duplicate filenames across repository source trees triggered IllegalDuplicateFile errors during automatic multi-document asset mapping
    - Constrained automatic asset discovery strictly to .clanker subdirectories within both the clanker repository and PUD workspace, eliminating broad root directory scans and unintended source code collisions
    - Introduced a new full-path-file-retrieval resolver type to enable explicit fetching of files outside .clanker using repository-relative paths
    - Updated FileBridge.getAssetMap() to target .clanker directories, ensuring collision checks apply exclusively within managed .clanker folders on a repository-by-repository basis

XXII: PORTS AND ADAPTERS ARCHITECTURE IMPLEMENTATION
    - Extracted concrete implementation bridges into a standalone adapters.py module
    - Defined abstract FileBridgePort and IOBridgePort interfaces in clanker.py inheriting from Bridge(ABC)
    - Updated concrete adapters (FileBridge, IOBridge) to implement their respective port interfaces
    - Restructured core services (SessionService, AssemblyService, IOService, GameEngine) around explicit constructor injection (__init__)
    - Configured main() as the Composition Root to lazily import and wire adapters into services at runtime

XXIII: LAYOUT TERMINOLOGY AND LAYOUT SOURCING REFACTOR
    - Removed get_clanker_files from FileBridgePort and Adapter interface
    - Declared Layout enum for centralized asset path management including UI and PROMPT layouts
    - Refactored FileBridgePort.read_clanker_asset to accept string layout paths and return raw content
    - Updated AssemblyService.get_template to resolve layouts dynamically via Layout enum members
    - Eliminated in-script template fallback constants BUILTIN_TEMPLATES, UI_TEMPL, and PROMPT_TEMPLATE


XXIV: REFACTOR UI BUTTON TEMPLATE SOURCING TO FILE READS
    - Migrated UI template button sourcing from in-script constants to dynamic file reads via Layout enum
    - Added BTN_ACTIVE, BTN_HL, and BTN_INACTIVE layout definitions to Layout enum
    - Updated AssemblyService._resolve (KB_INFO resolver) to read button templates using files.read_clanker_asset
    - Removed legacy in-script button template constants and deprecated keyboard.build_ui_repl_map

XXV: ELIMINATED RUAMEL FROM CLANKER.PY & FIXED WORKSPACE INITIALIZATION
    - Declared CfgFragments enum to cleanly handle configuration fragment paths and eliminated in-script yaml loader constants
    - Refactored FileBridge and FileBridgePort to accept string paths and support dedicated configuration fragment methods
    - Implemented DocPaths enum and dynamic document creation via write_default_documents for robust workspace initialization

XXVI: REFACTORED SESSION SERVICE CONFIGURATION LOADING
    - Replaced legacy path operations in SessionService.get_keyboard with structured CfgFragments lookups
    - Offloaded configuration template loading and directory generation logic to adapter ports during workspace setup

XXVII: RESOLVED CRITICAL PUD INITIALIZATION BUG VIA NAMESPACE REFACTOR
    - Fixed a critical initialization bug where progress documentation files were omitted from fresh .clanker setups due to raw enum values being passed to adapter methods
    - Refactored legacy enum-inheriting classes (CfgFragments, DocPaths, Layout, SystemKeys) into simple namespace classes to decouple raw string representations
    - Streamlined workspace bootstrapping by ensuring clean string path consumption across file bridge adapters

XXVIII: FIXED UI BORDER SHIFT BUG VIA BUTTON REPL MAP FIX
    - Corrected row indexation and text replacement logic in Button.get_repl_map
    - Stabilized UI layout integrity by ensuring consistent boundary rendering regardless of button state shifts

XXIX: IMPLEMENTED RESOLVER INCLUDE/EXCLUDE ERROR HANDLING
    - Updated REPO_CONTENT resolver callsite to pass missing_ok=False for include paths and missing_ok=True for exclude paths
    - Updated FileBridgePort interface signature and file bridge implementation to support the missing_ok parameter on get_pud_files

XXX: IMPROVED EX BASECLASS SYSTEM
    - Added 'UserNotice' base class to carry string messages for user presentation
    - Renamed 'Notice' to 'ControlNotice' / 'FlowNotice' to prohibit argument passing

XXXI: MOVED CONFIG PARSING RESPONSIBILITY TO CONFIGVALIDATOR
    - Split file bridge methods into raw string-fetching functions (`pud_file_as_string` and `shared_file_as_string`)
    - Created `utilities.py` housing `ConfigValidator` to encapsulate raw configuration parsing logic
    - Defined `ConfigValidatorProtocol` in the core layer and injected the concrete validator into `SessionService`
    - Updated call sites to acquire raw strings, validate them, and catch/reraise `ConfigViolations` as `UserTask` failures

XXXII: IMPLEMENTED RUNTIME CONFIGURATION SELECTIVE QUOTE ENFORCEMENT
    - Implemented helper `_assert_no_quotes` in `ConfigValidator` (`utilities.py`) to enforce strict selective quote restrictions on raw configuration files
    - Added line-by-line validation to flag double quotes and invalid single quote pairings
    - Accumulated violating lines into an actionable list with target filepath headers and indented entries
    - Raised a `ConfigViolations` instance containing the formatted error message whenever violations were detected

XXXIII: STREAMLINED CONFIG FRAGMENT LOADING VIA BASE PATH TOKENS AND SESSION SERVICE HELPER
    - Introduced BasePathTokens class defining basepath prefix tokens (PUD, SHARED) and updated CfgFragments path definitions
    - Updated FileBridge and FileBridgePort to combine separate file string methods into a unified get_file_contents method resolving basepath tokens dynamically
    - Added _get_validated_cfg_fragment helper method to SessionService to encapsulate raw content loading, quote validation, dictionary conversion, and exception handling
    - Refactored call sites across SessionService (get_keyboard, initialize_workspace) to utilize the centralized validation helper

XXXIV: ENFORCE PER-FILE VALIDATION AGAINST DUPLICATE INLINE FILESETS
    - Implemented assert_filesets_not_neglected in ConfigValidator to detect inline filesets matching top-level named sets
    - Refactored SessionService._get_validated_cfg_fragment to enforce a strict sequence of raw-text assertions, dictionary conversion, and dict-based assertions
    - Raised ConfigViolations detailing specific offending domains and renders when duplicate inline filesets are detected

XXXV: REFACTOR FILEBRIDGE FILE RETRIEVAL AND BASEPATH TOKENS
    - Refactored `get_pud_files` to `get_files` supporting tokenized argument payloads across `FileBridge` and `FileBridgePort`
    - Removed trailing slashes from `BasePathTokens` members (e.g., `"<PUD>/"` to `"<PUD>"`) and aligned `CfgFragments` members to include leading slashes
    - Aligned `FileBridge.get_file_contents` to accept the updated token and path string formats
    - Refactored `AssemblyService` `REPO_CONTENT` resolver branch to call `self.files.get_files(BasePathTokens.PUD, ...)`

XXXVI: ADD REPO_MANIFEST RESOLVER AND FILE MANIFEST BUILDER
    - Added REPO_MANIFEST ("repo-manifest") to Resolver.Type enum
    - Implemented _build_manifest_block helper method in AssemblyService to support file and fileset manifest generation
    - Added REPO_MANIFEST branch to AssemblyService._resolve supporting mandatory pud-manifest and optional shared-manifest blocks

XXXVII: RELOCATE TEMPLATE ASSETS AND UPDATE PATH CONSTANTS
    - Relocated template assets from `.clanker/shared-assets/templates` to `.clanker/templates`
    - Updated `DocPaths.SHARED_TEMPLATES` to `".clanker/templates/documentation"`
    - Updated `CfgFragments.TEMPLATE_CFG` to `BasePathTokens.SHARED + "/.clanker/templates/config.template"`

XXXVIII: FILEBRIDGE AND ADAPTER TOKENIZED PATH NORMALIZATION
    - Refactored `Config.DEFAULT_REL_PATH` to hold a plain string `/.clanker/config.yaml`
    - Refactored `write_yaml` methods across `clanker.py` and adapters to accept tokenized strings
    - Updated call sites to supply concatenated tokenized paths (e.g., `BasePathTokens.PUD + Config.DEFAULT_REL_PATH`)
    - Pruned unused `write_content` methods from the file bridge and its adapter implementations
    - Removed the lingering legacy `Config.DEFAULT_ASSETS_DIR` member

XXXIX: FILEBRIDGE AND ADAPTER TOKENIZED PATH NORMALIZATION CODEBASE MIGRATION
    - Combined `read_clanker_asset` and `read_pud_asset` into `read_asset` across `FileBridgePort` and its implementations
    - Updated `AssemblyService.get_template` to prepend `BasePathTokens.SHARED` onto layout paths
    - Aligned `AssemblyService._resolve` calls to consistently prepend `BasePathTokens.PUD` or `BasePathTokens.SHARED`
    - Refactored `AssemblyService._build_manifest_block` to eliminate token if/else branching
    - Normalized all path constants in Section 3 classes to start with '/' and removed embedded token strings
    - Updated all callsites to assemble paths dynamically using `BasePathTokens.X + Y.Z` logic

XL: FILEBRIDGE AND ASSEMBLYSERVICE PUD FALLBACK ASSET RETRIEVAL
    - Implemented `get_contents_with_pud_fallback` on FileBridge to resolve files against SHARED and PUD with collision checks
    - Updated FileBridgePort interface to include `get_contents_with_pud_fallback` and removed deprecated `getAssetMap` and `getFileContent`
    - Updated AssemblyService._resolve MULTI_DOC handler to leverage `get_contents_with_pud_fallback` for batch asset retrieval and fallback handling

XLI: LEVERAGE PORTS & ADAPTERS SPLIT -> OFFLOAD NON-BUSINESS LOGIC
    - Added new `ContentShaper` protocol class defining file specification normalization and tail truncation behaviors
    - Created implementing class `DefaultContentShaper` in `utilities.py` to house extracted file spec and tail truncation logic
    - Updated `clanker.py` main function to wire `DefaultContentShaper` into `AssemblyService` via dependency injection
    - Removed obsolete internal helper methods `_extract_file_spec` and `_apply_tail_truncation` from `AssemblyService` in favor of adapter delegation

XLII: SESSION SERVICE REFACTOR & CONFIG ACQUISITION
    - Refactored `SessionService.get_keyboard` into distinct acquisition and execution phases
    - Implemented strict two-block configuration fragment acquisition enforcing no fallbacks and raising `NoConfig` or `ConfigAssemblyFailure` appropriately
    - Rationalized defensive coding and consolidated declarations at the start of the execution phase

XLIII: WORKSPACE INITIALIZATION & TEMPLATE HYDRATION CLEANUP
    - Refactored `SessionService.initialize_workspace` exception handling to narrowly catch `FileNotFoundError` and raise `ConfigAssemblyFailure`
    - Delegated template hydration in `AssemblyService.hydrate` to the `ContentShaper` adapter

XLIV: ASSEMBLY SERVICE & FILEBRIDGE REFACTORING
    - Refactored `AssemblyService.get_template` layout path assignments to directly evaluate `self.files.read_asset` within match cases under single error handling
    - Absorbed `clear` functionality directly into `write` within `Filebridge`, eliminating the obsolete method and refactoring `IOService.get_confirmation` to maintain terminal output integrity

XLV: IOSERVICE & IOBRIDGE METHOD CLEANUP
    - Added `IOControl` class encapsulating terminal interaction control constants
    - Streamlined `SystemKeys` by delegating key control constants to `IOControl`
    - Offloaded character input validation and confirmation phrase matching logic to `IOBridge.get_acceptance`
    - Refactored `IOService.get_confirmation` into a multi-phase flow with explicit decline/invalid state handling

XLVI: SERVICE MEMBER REVIEW & AUDIT (PART 1)
    - Processed and evaluated core methods in `SessionService`, `AssemblyService`, and `IOService`
    - Confirmed narrow exception handling and core visibility priorities in `SessionService.initialize_workspace`
    - Standardized `AssemblyService.hydrate` to delegate text shaping and transformation to `ContentShaper`
    - Verified operational integrity across input/output methods in `IOService` (`display`, `to_clipboard`, `get_key`, `get_confirmation`)

XLVII: RUNTIME CONFIG ASSEMBLER ADAPTER & MODEL EXTRACTION
    - Extracted object graph assembly from SessionService to dedicated RuntimeConfigAssembler adapter matching RuntimeConfigAssemblerProtocol
    - Refactored SessionService.get_keyboard into a 3-phase orchestrator delegating setup to file acquisition, validation, and assembly
    - Relocated domain models and SystemKeys into models.py to fix type verification issues across domain-attached resolvers

XLVIII: DATACLASS MODEL MIGRATION & RUNTIME CONFIG ASSEMBLER
    - Converted core application models (`Resolver`, `Render`, `Domain`, `Button`, `Keyboard`) from Pydantic to standard `@dataclass` classes in `models.py`
    - Removed all Pydantic dependencies and configuration structures from the domain models
    - Implemented bottom-up object tree instantiation via `RuntimeConfigAssembler` in `utilities.py` to decouple configuration loading and mapping

XLIX: RUNTIME CONFIGURATION CONTAINER & BOUNDARY ALIGNMENT
    - Implemented RuntimeConfig root dataclass holding keyboard, ui_render, and base_resolvers to establish clean configuration boundaries
    - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler and ConfigValidator to process filesets, evict resolvers from system config, and load global base_resolvers from shared config
    - Wired RuntimeConfig through SessionService and GameEngine, refactoring prompt compilation and UI rendering to consume the new config model
    - Aligned YAML schemas and filenames (renaming kb_def.yaml to system_cfg.yaml and shared_domains.yaml to shared_cfg.yaml)

L: BUTTON MODEL ALIGNMENT & LEGACY CODE REMOVAL
    - Aligned the Button and Keyboard models by renaming primary properties to key and action, while removing legacy secondary fields and shift-action bindings
    - Cleaned up key handling and service normalization in clanker.py, simplifying keyboard dispatch and updating KB_INFO resolution to use single key sequences
    - Refactored RuntimeConfigAssembler in utilities.py to construct buttons using single key mappings without secondary configurations
    - Removed all secondary row properties and key mappings from the system_cfg.yaml schema

LI: INTRODUCE PROMPT MODEL WRAPPER AND ALIGN DOMAIN/RENDER HIERARCHY
    - Defined Prompt(name: str, renders: list[Render]) dataclass in models.py
    - Updated Domain model to replace renders with prompts: list[Prompt] and Render to remove name and default template
    - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler and GameEngine to construct and consume Prompt models and single/multi-render structures
    - Aligned shared_cfg.yaml and config.yaml schemas to nest render definitions under Prompt objects

LII: ALIGN BUTTON AND PROMPT DOMAIN MODELS FOR SINGLE-RENDER ARCHITECTURE
    - Updated Button.inhabitant type hint to Domain | Prompt | None in models.py
    - Renamed Prompt.renders to singular Prompt.render (Render) and adjusted RuntimeConfigAssembler parsing
    - Refactored clanker.py GameEngine to read directly from btn.inhabitant.render
    - Aligned shared_cfg.yaml and config.yaml configurations to the single render structure
    - improved 'history-output-instructions.md' for better workflow

LIII: RESOLVER DOMAIN MODEL REFACTORING & POLYMORPHIC RESOLUTION
    - Introduced FileSet, TruncationSpec, File, and Filelist models in models.py
    - Created typed Resolver base class and subclasses (MultiDocResolver, RepoContentResolver, ManifestResolver, KBStateResolver)
    - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler, AssemblyService, and configuration schemas to support typed resolver structures

LIV: REFACTOR RESOLVER DOMAIN MODELS TO PURE DATA CLASSES & MIGRATE RESOLUTION LOGIC
    - Converted Resolver hierarchy in models.py to pure configuration data classes holding attributes and anchor
    - Moved all resolution and hydration dispatching into AssemblyService inside clanker.py via type-matched helpers (_res_multi_doc, _res_repo_content, _res_manifest, _res_ui)
    - Consolidated manifest block creation under AssemblyService._build_manifest

LV: DATA MODEL REVAMP & UNUSED ALT-MODE REMOVAL CONCLUDED
    - Eliminated Pydantic dependencies in favor of native Python dataclass representations across models.py
    - Restructured AssemblyService resolver dispatch and resolution helpers to work with pure dataclass instances

LVI: ARCHITECTURAL EVALUATION: SEPARATE ENTRYPOINT FILE (REJECTED)
    - Evaluated extracting a dedicated entrypoint module to centralize repeated model imports
    - Proposal rejected due to minimal benefit for application scope and preference for existing import patterns

LVII: EXCEPTION HIERARCHY OVERHAUL & MODELS MIGRATION
    - Decoupled exception rules from base class hierarchy into ExceptionPolicy convenience class in clanker.py
    - Restructured BaseEx in models.py using abstract leaf_ex property to enforce non-leaf class non-instantiability
    - Migrated all concrete and intermediate exception declarations (Failure, ControlNotice, UserNotice, etc.) to models.py

LVIII: ADAPTER EXCEPTION POLICY DECOUPLING & BRIDGE REMOVAL
    - Introduced ExceptionPolicy.protect_adapter in clanker.py to dynamically decorate adapter instance methods with wrap_bridge_call
    - Eliminated Bridge base class and converted IOBridgePort and FileBridgePort to inherit directly from ABC/Protocol
    - Updated entrypoint main() to wrap adapter instances via ExceptionPolicy during initialization

LIX: PROTOCOL UNIFICATION FOR ADAPTER PORTS & UTILITIES
    - Centralized all port and utility interface specifications in models.py using typing.Protocol
    - Migrated FileBridgePort, IOBridgePort, ContentShaperProtocol, ConfigValidatorProtocol, and RuntimeConfigAssemblerProtocol to models.py
    - Maintained zero internal module import constraints in models.py while updating clanker.py service dependencies to structural typing

LX: IMPORT RATIONALIZATION & DEPENDENCY CLEANUP COMPLETION
    - Centralized shared domain models, path tokens, layout constants, and exception hierarchies inside models.py
    - Restructured module imports across utilities.py and adapters.py to depend strictly on models.py
    - Eliminated circular imports and clanker.py dependencies in peripheral modules following Bridge removal and protocol unification

LXI: ENGINE AND GAMEENGINE CONSOLIDATION
    - Merged base class `Engine` into `GameEngine` and renamed the unified class to `AppEngine` to remove the informational baseclass experiment and reduce indirection
    - Eliminated pass-through helpers (`_add_to_board` and `_dispatch_cmd`) in favor of in-line logic within the execution run method
    - Retained targeted workflow helper methods (`_bootstrap`, `_display_ui`, `_wire_num_row`, `_set_selected_num_btn`, `_compile_to_clipboard`, and `_render`)

LXII: MOVE SHARED DOMAINS TO ASDF ROW AND SUPPORT DUAL DOMAIN ROWS
    - Added explicit row semantics (Button.TYPE_DOMAIN, Button.TYPE_PROMPT) inside models.py to remove magic strings
    - Updated system_cfg.yaml row definitions and layout mapping to support dual domain rows (shared domains and pud domains) with optimized keyboard ergonomics
    - Refactored RuntimeConfigAssembler in utilities.py to organize assembly into distinct acquisition, consumption, and finalization phases
    - Enhanced AppEngine and AssemblyService in clanker.py to handle dual domain row state, selection clearing, and UI resolution correctly

LXIII: DTO-DRIVEN CONFIG INGESTION AND BOUNDARY VALIDATION [FEATURE]
    - Goal: Replace raw dictionary access across configuration parsing with a strongly typed DTO abstraction layer and establish a strict failfast boundary at configuration ingestion to eliminate downstream defensive code and fallbacks.
    - Phase 1: SystemConfigDataDTO Ingestion
        - Introduced SystemConfigDataDTO to replace raw dict access during keyboard and base render construction in RuntimeConfigAssembler.
        - Flattened system_cfg.yaml structure to align directly with typed fields.
    - Phase 2: DTOFactory Extraction
        - Extracted parsing logic out of SystemConfigDataDTO.from_dict into a dedicated DTOFactory.sys_cfg method.
        - Wired RuntimeConfigAssembler to utilize DTOFactory instance for initial config mapping.
    - Phase 3: RenderDTO Introduction
        - Defined RenderDTO for render configurations and added DTOFactory.render_cfg.
        - Refactored base render and resolver initialization inside RuntimeConfigAssembler to consume RenderDTO.
    - Phase 4: ResolverDTO Abstraction
        - Defined initial ResolverDTO and factory method resolver_cfg handling anchor and fileset mapping.
        - Implemented assembler resolver dispatch helper mapping typed DTOs to domain Resolver instances.
    - Phase 5: DomainDTO Integration
        - Defined DomainDTO and added DTOFactory.domain_cfg.
        - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler with _build_domains to construct domain models strictly via DTO pipelines.
    - Phase 6: PromptDTO Integration
        - Defined PromptDTO and DTOFactory.prompt_cfg.
        - Added _build_prompts in assembler to encapsulate prompt creation through DTO transformations.
    - Phase 7: Named FileSet Mapping
        - Implemented _build_named_filesets in assembler to resolve PUD vs shared fileset precedence rules.
        - Updated RepoContentResolver and ManifestResolver construction logic to consume resolved named filesets.
    - Phase 8: ResolverDTO Hierarchy Specialization
        - Refactored ResolverDTO into specialized subclasses: MultiDocResolverDTO, RepoContentResolverDTO, ManifestResolverDTO, and KBStateResolverDTO.
        - Updated DTOFactory.resolver_cfg to delegate to specialized private parsing methods (_mdr_cfg, _repo_cfg, _manif_cfg, _ui_cfg).
    - Phase 9: FileSetDTO Standardization
        - Defined FileSetDTO and added DTOFactory.fileset_cfg.
        - Refactored _build_fileset to instantiate domain FileSet directly from FileSetDTO.
    - Phase 10: Complete File-Level DTO Coverage
        - Defined TruncationSpecDTO, FileDTO, and FilelistDTO alongside Tier 1 factory methods.
        - Updated MultiDocResolverDTO and assembler file construction routines to process file lists via typed DTO chains.
    - Failfast Policy Validation Accumulator
        - Established DTOFactory as the definitive fail-fast boundary for all incoming YAML config inputs.
        - Implemented strict type assertion helpers (req_str, req_dict, req_list, req_bool, req_int, req_str_or_dict) to immediately raise errors on invalid or missing properties.
        - Completely removed fallback defaults across all DTO factory methods to guarantee downstream type safety and eliminate defensive handling in assembly code.
    - Note: While this feature successfully establishes complete type safety and insulates domain models from raw dictionary structures, it introduces noticeable boilerplate and visual bloat inside config_dtos.py. 
      This complexity is properly contained within the DTO boundary, but future structural consolidation may be desirable.

LXIV: REFACTOR CONFIG ASSEMBLY - TRANSITION DTOFACTORY TO CONFIGTRANSLATOR
    - Strategy: Establish the new ConfigTranslator contract with the config validator while keeping DTOFactory onboard as a transitory implementation detail to cap job scope.
    - Created ConfigTranslator to handle extraction logic (extract_filesets, extract_domains, process_sys_cfg) and domain model instantiation.
    - Kept existing DTOFactory methods intact internally to avoid broad cascading changes across raw DTO parsing.
    - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler to assemble runtime configuration via KbSpec and precedence-aware fileset resolution.

LXV: SMELLFIX & TRANSLATOR PROTOCOL REFACTOR
    - Defined ConfigTranslatorProtocol in utilities.py as the consumer-side interface for RuntimeConfigAssembler.
    - Added public get_resolvers method to ConfigTranslator in config_dtos.py to satisfy the protocol contract.
    - Updated RuntimeConfigAssembler to call get_resolvers instead of accessing private translator methods, and reordered base_resolvers resolution to run immediately after fileset_map.

LXVI: CONFIG TRANSLATION & MODEL CLEANLINESS BUSINESS
    - Updated TruncationSpec in models.py to mandate an explicit integer for tail_lines, and updated FileSet to require explicit lists for includes and excludes.
    - Updated extract_filesets in config_dtos.py to use req_dict with default={}, and extract_domains to use req_list without fallback to enforce domain presence.
    - Refactored truncation_spec_cfg in config_dtos.py to use req_int with default=None instead of manual key presence guards.

LXVII: REMOVE FULL-PATH FILE RETRIEVAL FUNCTIONALITY FROM MULTIDOCRESOLVER STACK
    - Stripped full_path_from_pud attribute from File dataclass in models.py
    - Removed full-path retrieval logic, res_type aliases, and DTO attributes from config_dtos.py
    - Removed full_path_from_pud conditional branch in AssemblyService._res_multi_doc within clanker.py to enforce standardized name-based fallback lookup

LXVIII: RATIONALIZE CONFIG TRANSLATION AND DTO LAYER
    - Replaced DTOFactory with ValueExtractor featuring path extraction and type enforcement methods (req_str, req_dict, req_list, etc.)
    - Updated ConfigTranslator to map raw configuration dicts directly into domain models via ValueExtractor
    - Eliminated intermediate DTO classes (SysCfgDTO, RenderDTO, ResolverDTO hierarchy, TruncationSpecDTO, FileDTO, FilelistDTO, DomainDTO, PromptDTO, FileSetDTO)
    - Retained KbSpec for UI key assignment transport and preserved ConfigTranslatorProtocol compatibility in utilities.py

LXIX: INTEGRATE CROSS-LAYER ERROR AGGREGATION AND STREAMLINE CONFIGURATION PIPELINE
    - Implemented `ErrorCollector` with path stack tracing for comprehensive configuration assembly error handling
    - Refactored `ConfigTranslator` and `FilesetMap` to handle stateful merging and clean internal dictionary extractions
    - Cleaned up `RuntimeConfigAssembler` execution flow to natively manage error collection and simplify translator protocols

LXX: INTRODUCE SINGLE-USE RUNTIME CONFIG BUILDER PATTERN
    - Replaced `RuntimeConfigAssembler` with a single-use `RuntimeConfigBuilder` class in `utilities.py` to streamline the configuration lifecycle
    - Extracted core assembly steps into dedicated helper methods (`_handle_named_filesets`, `_handle_domains`, and `_handle_buttons`) storing intermediate state on self
    - Refactored `clanker.py` and `SessionService` to instantiate `RuntimeConfigBuilder` directly, leveraging `.build()` to return both collector and configuration instances to `AppEngine`

LXXI: EXPAND TRUNCATIONSPEC TO SUPPORT TAIL AND REGEX-BASED SLICING
    - Expanded `TruncationSpec` model to support mutually exclusive `tail` (via `tail_lines`) and `regex_range` (via `from_line` and `up_to`) truncation strategies
    - Refactored `ContentShaper` protocol and `DefaultContentShaper` to replace `trim_to_tail` with `apply_truncation` for unified truncation handling
    - Updated `ConfigTranslator` to validate truncation configuration exclusivity and regex pattern requirements using `ErrorCollector`
    - Refactored `AssemblyService._res_multi_doc` in `clanker.py` to delegate file content slicing directly to `ContentShaper.apply_truncation`
    - Enabled targeted slicing of document sections (such as backlog segments), enabling leaner and more tailored prompts for optimized LLM context usage

LXXII: RESTRUCTURE APPLICATION INTO SUBSYSTEM-BASED ARCHITECTURE
    - Restructured application file hierarchy by establishing `content` as the root directory for all source files, laying groundwork for repository contract isolation
    - Introduced subsystem-level contract system via adjacent `contracts` directory (`assembly_system_contract.py`, `ports.py`, `render_system_contract.py`), decoupling consumer dependencies using Python `Protocol` definitions
    - Partitioned internal architecture into modular subsystem components under `content`, including `config_assembly_system`, `render_pipeline`, `adapters`, `contracts`, `models.py`, and main entry point `clanker.py`
    - Refactored `clanker.py` imports and module dependencies to align with the new nested subsystem topology

LXXIII: EXCEPTION SYSTEM REVISION AND EXCEPTION POLICY CONSOLIDATION
    - Refactored core exception hierarchy in models.py: renamed Failure to Fatal, ControlNotice to Notice, and pruned obsolete exception types (UserNotice, BaseExInstantiation, BadFile, NotImplemented, MissedAdoptedNotice, ConfigViolations)
    - Enhanced NoticeArgs(Fatal) to accept class name, positional arguments, and keyword arguments for improved diagnostics when Notice classes are instantiated with parameters
    - Updated ExceptionPolicy.reraise_as_failure in clanker.py to handle Notice instances and ADOPTED_NOTICES uniformly, re-raising them as MissedNotice failures

LXXIV: THREE-PILLAR EXCEPTION POLICY FRAMING AND DYNAMIC EXCEPTION FORMATTING
    - Implemented `ExceptionPolicy.protect_adapter` (Gate 1) to wrap public adapter methods and transform untrusted third-party errors into `BridgeLeakage` fatal exceptions while allowing `Notice` instances to pass through
    - Retained `ExceptionPolicy.reraise_as_failure` (Gate 2) to trap uncaught internal domain exceptions into `MissedNotice` or `UnexpectedEx` fatal failures
    - Updated `Fatal` base exception string representation to prepend dynamic separators and added custom `BridgeLeakage.__str__` formatting to dynamically extract and report underlying `__cause__` details
    - Implemented `ExceptionPolicy.print_traceback_and_exit` (Pillar 3) to print a high-level `[FATAL]` failure summary header before dumping the underlying cause traceback to stderr and exiting

LXXV: APPENGINE EXECUTION AND EXCEPTION CONTROL FLOW REFINEMENT
    - Updated ProgramExit exception model in models.py by deprecating get_compliance_msg() in favor of direct ClassVar strings (MSG_DEFAULT and MSG_DECLINED_INIT)
    - Refined AppEngine._bootstrap in clanker.py to allow exceptions to bubble up directly to caller
    - Restructured AppEngine.run into two sequential phase try blocks (Phase 1: Bootstrap & Init, Phase 2: UI Loop) with explicit exception handling for initialization confirmation, declines, and standard UI exits

LXXVI: REFACTOR EXCEPTION POLICY FOR APPENGINE INTERPRETATION AND MAIN FALLBACK
    - Replaced `ExceptionPolicy.reraise_as_failure` and `print_traceback_and_exit` with `interpret_as_fatal` to standardize incoming exceptions to fatal types and return formatted string representations with underlying stack traces
    - Refactored `AppEngine.run` to catch unhandled execution exceptions internally, process them via `ExceptionPolicy.interpret_as_fatal`, and return formatted fatal strings
    - Simplified `main()` execution flow to print `engine.run()` directly within a generic fallback catch block for critical exception architecture failures

LXXVII: TRANSITION INTERFACE LAYER FROM STATIC PROTOCOLS TO RUNTIME-ENFORCED ABS
    - Shifted structural duck-typing to explicit nominal contracts across the codebase using Python's native `ABC` and `@abstractmethod` to enforce runtime guarantees without relying on external static analysis tools
    - Converted interface contracts in `content/contracts/ports.py` (`IOBridgePort`, `FileBridgePort`, `ConfigIngestorPort`), `content/contracts/assembly_system_contract.py` (`RtcAssembler`, `Report`), and `content/contracts/render_system_contract.py` (`ContentShaper`) from Protocols to Abstract Base Classes
    - Aligned concrete implementations in adapters (`FileBridge`, `IOBridge`, `ConfigIngestor`), the assembly component (`RuntimeConfigAssembler`, `ErrorCollector`), and the render pipeline (`DefaultContentShaper`) to explicitly inherit from their respective port and subsystem ABC contracts

LXXVIII: TRANSITION INTERFACE LAYER FROM STATIC PROTOCOLS TO RUNTIME-ENFORCED ABCS
    - Shifted structural duck-typing to explicit nominal contracts to enforce runtime guarantees without relying on external static analysis tools
    - Converted translation interface contracts in `content/config_assembly_system/contracts/translation_contract.py` (`FilesetMapABC`, `ConfigTranslatorABC`) from Protocols to Abstract Base Classes using native `ABC` and `@abstractmethod`
    - Aligned concrete implementations (`FilesetMap`, `ConfigTranslator`) in `content/config_assembly_system/translation_system/config_dtos.py` to inherit from their respective ABC contracts
    - Concluded current interface iteration pending future exploration of a custom `.bind` approach to mimic Go-style dependency binding

LXXIX: IMPLEMENT COMPREHENSIVE DOMAIN OVERFLOW HANDLING AND CAPACITY COMPLAINT CONSUMPTION
    - Modeled `DomainOverflow` in `content/config_assembly_system/code.py` to capture overflow details and generate formatted complaint strings
    - Integrated `DomainOverflow` storage, registration, and report generation into `ErrorCollector` within `content/config_assembly_system/translation_system/config_dtos.py`
    - Added `@abstractmethod get_domain_overflow_report(self) -> str | None` to the `Report` ABC in `content/contracts/assembly_system_contract.py`
    - Refined runtime config assembly to detect capacity exceedances during button mapping, record overflow complaints, and safely omit overflowing domains
    - Updated session services and application bootstrapping in `clanker.py` to check for domain overflow reports and prompt the user for bootstrap acceptance or exit

LXXX: REFACTOR APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE BY DECOUPLING SERVICES, RESTRUCTURING ADAPTERS, AND ORGANIZING APP LAYERS
    - Relocated low-level infrastructure typing and bridge interfaces to 'adapters/ports.py', keeping them separate from application logic
    - Moved core domain models, system exceptions, and base data structures into 'app/models.py' to isolate fundamental types alongside the core engine
    - Refactored 'clanker.py' strictly into a composition root managing adapter instantiation, exception policy wrapping, dependency injection, and engine execution
    - Renamed SessionService to IngestionService and relocated it inside the 'asset_ingestion' module directory alongside its supporting files
    - Renamed AssemblyService to RenderService and relocated it inside the 'render_pipeline' module directory to align with hydration responsibilities
    - Renamed IOService to TUIService and relocated it inside the 'tui' module directory to accurately reflect terminal user interface operations

LXXXI: IMPLEMENT SEQUENTIAL CONFIGURATION ASSEMBLY PIPELINE WITH EPHEMERAL WORKERS
    Purpose: Refactor runtime configuration assembly into modular, single-responsibility workers to decouple extraction logic and enforce robust error tracking.
    Actions:
    - Implemented FilesetExtractor worker with ValueExtractor composition to extract shared and PUD filesets into a unified FilesetMap.
    - Implemented DomainExtractor worker to encapsulate domain, prompt, render, and resolver parsing logic.
    - Implemented RtcAssembler worker to parse keyboard layout specifications, map button actions, and report domain overflow issues via ErrorCollector.
    - Extracted UIRenderExtractor to independently pull UI render templates from system configuration.
    - Extracted BaseResolverExtractor to parse multi-document retrieval base resolvers from non-system configurations.
    - Re-wired IngestionServiceImpl.get_runtime_config to orchestrate worker execution in a structured pipeline.
    Reflection:
    - Ephemeral worker delegation isolated config extraction responsibilities, eliminated monolithic DTO parsing debt, and simplified error collection across pipeline stages.
    - Need to determine an optimal strategy for deduplicating shared worker logic without introducing pipeline nesting or tight coupling.

LXXXII: CONSOLIDATE CONFIGURATION ASSEMBLY AROUND EPHEMERAL WORKERS AND PARSERS
    Purpose: Complete the restructuring of runtime configuration assembly into a sequential pipeline of focused extractors and assemblers, while separating entity parsing from validation policy and complaint handling.
    - Consolidate resolver construction behind ResolverWorker and fileset construction behind FilesetWorker, removing duplicated parsing and construction logic from higher-level extractors.
    - Refactor RenderWorker, DomainExtractor, BaseResolverExtractor, and FilesetExtractor to delegate entity construction to the appropriate lower-level workers/parsers.
    - Add ErrorCollector.path context management to simplify path-stack handling and ensure complaint context is correctly restored.
    - Enforce ui_render validation at the extractor boundary, requiring exactly one KBStateResolver ('kb_info').
    - Align extractors and assemblers with the service so each performs a focused, one-call delivery into the sequential configuration assembly pipeline.
    - Establish a clearer division whereby parsers perform local configuration validation and complaint production, while extractors and assemblers determine which configuration issues become meaningful complaints at the pipeline level.
    Reflection: The ingestion architecture now has substantially clearer responsibility boundaries and a more compositional configuration assembly flow, reducing monolithic parsing and cognitive load. The new structure should now be allowed to settle and prove itself through continued use and validation before introducing another major architectural restructuring.

LXXXIII: TAIL-TRUNCATE PROJECT HISTORY FOR BRAGPACK ASSEMBLY
    Purpose: Reduce token pressure and confusion by keeping only recent history.
    Actions: Updated the GitHub Action to tail-truncate the history document to ~12k characters.
    Reflection: History context is now bounded and focused on recent development.
    - but is dirty github action
    - to be replaced by project native solution, as we dont want to depend upon github when we can avoid it

LXXXIV: ADD ASSET EXISTS CHECK TO INGESTION PIPELINE
    Purpose: Validate asset existence across resolvers during ingestion and flag dangling prompt assets.
    - Resolvers must verify that referenced files/filesets exist in expected pathlists before runtime config assembly.
    - The pipeline must also detect unused/dangling prompt assets in the local configuration folder.
    Actions: Implemented AssetValidator and integrated it into IngestionServiceImpl.
    - Created ephemeral class 'AssetValidator' in 'content/asset_ingestion/validators/asset_validator.py' with static 'validate' method accepting pathlists, runtime config, and complaint collector.
    - Implemented resolver checks: MultiDocResolver checks pud/shared pathlists by file name; RepoContentResolver checks pud_pathlist for fileset paths; ManifestResolver checks pud_fileset in pud_pathlist and shared_fileset in shared_pathlist.
    - Integrated AssetValidator into 'content/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py' to run after file list retrieval and report complaints via collector.
    - Added inverse validation check to flag filepaths in '.clanker/prompt-assets' that are not referenced in the runtime config.
    Reflection: Verification now catches missing dependency files and orphaned prompt assets early during bootstrap before rendering.
    - but very janky 'toe in the water'
    - i will shift attention to the concept of repo contract

LXXXV: FIX ATTRIBUTEERROR CRASH ON OUT-OF-SCOPE KEYPRESS
    Purpose: Prevent application crashes when an unhandled or out-of-scope key is pressed during runtime.
    Actions: Guard 'self.msg' updates during key handling within the application engine.
    - Updated the event loop in 'app/engine.py' ('run') to store the result of 'handle_key' in a local variable.
    - Restricted reassignment of 'self.msg' to occur only when the key handling result is not None.
    Reflection: Key interaction loop is now more resilient against unmapped or ignored key inputs.

LXXXVI: CONFINE PATH TO ADAPTER LAYER AND IMPLEMENT EXCEPTION TRANSLATION
    Purpose: 
    - Move constant type classes out of models.py and into constants.py or adjacent to their primary callers.
    - Isolate `Path` imports exclusively to the adapter layer.
    - Make adapters responsible for translating their exception vocabulary into domain exception vocabulary.
    Actions: Refactored port boundaries, path constants, and filesystem error handling across layers.
    - Extracted application path constants (`CfgFragments`, `Layout`, `Config`, `BasePathTokens`) to `content/app/constants.py` and relocated TUI `IOControl`.
    - Removed `from __future__ import annotations` across the codebase.
    - Replaced `pathlib.Path` with string types in `FileBridgePort` signatures and `FileBridge` adapter methods.
    - Refactored `AssetValidator` to perform path validation exclusively using string path sets.
    - Defined `NoSuchFile` (Notice) and `FileAccessError` (Fatal) domain exceptions in `ports.py`.
    - Translated `FileNotFoundError`, `PermissionError`, and `UnicodeDecodeError` in `FileBridge` methods to domain exceptions.
    - Updated error handling in `IngestionServiceImpl` and `RenderServiceImpl` to consume `NoSuchFile`.
    - Simplified `ExceptionPolicy` in `app/engine.py` by removing `ADOPTED_NOTICES` and wrapping non-domain adapter errors in `AdapterLeakage`.
    Reflection: 
    - Achieved a partial breakup of godfile 'models.py' and grouped path-related constants in one file, making analysis and prompt context management easier.
    - Isolated `Path` to the adapter layer, forcing LLM discipline across core domain logic.
    - Aligned exception translation with Ports & Adapters architecture, allowing adapters to be cleanly swapped out without core dependencies on legacy 'ADOPTED_NOTICES'.

LXXXVII: PRUNE DANGLING ASSETS
    Purpose: Prune dangling asset files across the project workspace.
    Actions: Removed unused asset files identified during pipeline validation.
    - Deleted 5 unused assets referenced by configurations.
    Reflection: Demonstrated the practical value and efficacy of the recently updated ingestion and validation pipeline in identifying unreferenced workspace artifacts.

LXXXVIII: CENTRALIZE AND REFACTOR PATH CONSTANTS
    Purpose: Centralize path string construction and standardize path constant structures across the app to reduce string duplication and improve token handling.
    - Path definitions were previously fragmented or manually concatenated in multiple downstream consumers, creating risk of path string divergence.
    Actions:
    - Renamed constants classes `Layout` to `Layouts` and `BasePathTokens` to `PathTokens` in `constants.py`.
    - Standardized path members as plain pre-concatenated tokenized strings directly in `CfgFragments`, `Layouts`, and `DocPaths`.
    - Updated `RenderServiceImpl._res_ui` to leverage `Layouts` class members instead of inline string manipulation.
    - Updated `IngestionServiceImpl.initialize_workspace` and `FileBridge.write_default_documents` to pass and handle token-prefixed path constants natively.
    Reflection: Cleanly isolated token resolution logic to the adapter layer while establishing a predictable, pre-tokenized path schema across domain services without breaking file resolution logic.

LXXXIX: REORGANIZE SHARED ASSETS OUT OF CLANKER LOCAL DIRECTORY
    Purpose: Align Clanker's local workspace layout with standard PUD architecture and advance the repo contract vision by relocating shared assets out of .clanker into a unified library path.
    - Path references were tightly coupled to .clanker directory layouts, preventing Clanker itself from adhering to standard PUD structural expectations.
    Actions:
    - Relocated shared assets from '.clanker/shared-assets' to 'content/a_lib/shared-assets'.
    - Relocated shared templates from '.clanker/templates' to 'content/a_lib/templates'.
    - Cleaned up obsolete directories from the old location in '.clanker'.
    - Updated path constants across `CfgFragments`, `DocPaths`, and `Layouts` in `content/app/constants.py` to route through 'content/a_lib/'.
    Reflection: Cleanly decoupled shared application assets from local execution context; however, relocating prompt fragments broke existing `.md` resolver paths that relied on the former `.clanker` layout.

XC: SHARED ASSET RESOLUTION BUGFIX AND FILE BRIDGE CLEANUP
    Purpose: Ensure reliable fallbacks for shared asset lookups across the complete library path and eliminate redundant tokenized path slicing in the file adapter.
    - Tokenized path resolution logic was duplicated across multiple file adapter methods (`get_file_contents`, `write_yaml`, `read_asset`), while shared asset lookup failed on nested subdirectories in `clanker_path`.
    Actions:
    - Updated shared asset fallback lookup in `content/ports_adapters/adapters.py` to scan the full `clanker_path` while skipping hidden directories.
    - Implemented `_resolve_tokenized_path` private helper in `content/ports_adapters/adapters.py` to centralize `PathTokens.PUD` and `PathTokens.SHARED` prefix processing and map paths to corresponding `Path` objects.
    - Refactored `get_file_contents`, `write_yaml`, and `read_asset` methods to utilize `_resolve_tokenized_path`.
    Reflection: Cleaned up path-resolution code and guaranteed robust fallback asset retrieval; mechanics may undergo further refinement as the asset architecture evolves.

XCI: MODELS MODULE DECOMPOSITION AND ELIMINATION
    Purpose: Dismantle the 'models.py' god file by extracting domain entities, presentation models, and exceptions into dedicated application submodules.
    - 'models.py' accumulated mixed concerns ranging from domain dataclasses and UI layout/presentation state to application-wide exception hierarchies.
    Actions:
    - Extracted ActionResult presentation entity to 'content/app/presentation.py' and moved button replacement layout formatting logic to ContentShaper in the render pipeline.
    - Extracted the domain exception hierarchy (Fatal, Notice, BaseEx derivatives) to 'content/app/exceptions.py'.
    - Extracted pure data dataclasses (resolvers, specs, prompts, domain, buttons, runtime config) to 'content/app/entities.py'.
    - Deleted 'content/app/models.py' after migrating all members and refactored dependent imports across 'engine.py', 'render_service.py', and adapters.
    Reflection: Eliminates a central monolithic dependency, establishing clear boundaries between domain entities, exception handling, and presentation logic.

XCII: DECOUPLING PRESENTATION CONCERNS FROM DOMAIN ENTITIES
    Purpose: Isolate domain entity classes from rendering mechanics and UI formatting logic.
    - Domain entity classes (specifically 'Button') previously contained UI layout formatting logic and inline imports targeting the render pipeline.
    Actions:
    - Added 'shape_button_replacements' to 'content/render_pipeline/content_shaper.py' to handle line splitting, label padding, and delimiter replacement.
    - Refactored '_res_ui' in 'content/render_pipeline/render_service.py' to delegate button layout formatting directly to ContentShaper rather than invoking entity methods.
    - Stripped 'get_repl_map()' and associated render pipeline imports from 'Button' in 'content/app/entities.py'.
    Reflection: Re-established strict domain isolation by ensuring domain entities remain pure data containers stripped of presentation responsibilities.

XCIII: REFACTORING KEYBOARD MANAGEMENT INTO DEDICATED KBSERVICE AND REFINING SERVICE BOUNDARIES
    Purpose: Isolate keyboard state management and button orchestration into a dedicated service while decoupling presentation rendering dependencies via explicit context objects.
    - System state was tightly coupled to monolithic structures (`RuntimeConfig`, `Keyboard`) and `AppEngine` was directly managing button state wiring, key routing, and presentation formatting.
    Actions:
    - Dissolved `RuntimeConfig` and refactored `IngestionService` to return explicit config components (`Report`, `dict[str, Button]`, `Render`, `list[Resolver]`).
    - Introduced `KBService` (`KBServiceImpl`) to encapsulate key handling, domain/prompt button wiring, and selected key state management, replacing the legacy `Keyboard` class.
    - Defined `RenderContext` and `UIRenderContext` data transfer objects in `keyboard.py` to pass strict presentation state (`btn_map`, `selected_key`, `render`, `base_resolvers`) to `RenderService`.
    - Expanded `RenderService` to own UI and prompt rendering end-to-end via `render_ui` and `render_prompt`, absorbing button-shaping and template hydration logic.
    - Delegated clipboard formatting to `TUIServiceImpl.to_clipboard`, returning structured `ActionResult` objects.
    - Simplified `AppEngine` into a thin execution loop coordinating `KBService`, `RenderService`, and `TUIService`.
    Reflection: Cleanly separated domain state orchestration from presentation rendering, establishing strict service boundaries and removing stateful boilerplate from the main engine loop.

XCIV: LOCALIZED ENGINE EXECUTION STATE AND FORMALIZED ACTIONRESULT PRODUCTION IN SERVICES
    Purpose: Decouple presentation message formatting from engine state by introducing static message templates on ActionResult and localizing response lifecycle tracking within the AppEngine runtime.
    Actions:
    - Added static template string constants to `ActionResult` (`BOOTSTRAP_SUCCESS`, `NO_PROMPT_BOUND`, `UNBOUND_KEY`, `DOMAIN_SELECTED`, `KEY_EMPTY`, `COPIED_TO_CLIPBOARD`) and removed the dynamic `get_msg()` method in `presentation.py`.
    - Refactored `KBServiceImpl` methods (`handle_key`, `_set_selected_num_btn`, and `_create_render_context`) to produce structured `ActionResult` instances formatted with key/domain metadata.
    - Updated `TUIServiceImpl.to_clipboard` to calculate line/character counts and return a formatted `ActionResult.COPIED_TO_CLIPBOARD` object.
    - Adjusted `IngestionServiceImpl.get_runtime_config` to return an explicit `ActionResult` indicating bootstrap completion alongside runtime components.
    - Extended `ContentShaper` with `shape_action_result` to format, pad, and truncate action message strings to a uniform UI width (117 chars).
    - Updated `RenderServiceImpl.render_ui` to shape raw `ActionResult.message` content directly during UI rendering.
    - Eliminated `self.msg` instance state from `AppEngine`, converting action results into scoped local variables (`action_res`) passed dynamically across the application loop and renderer.
    Reflection: Cleanly transferred responsibility for action feedback generation to services, enabling pure value flow through the execution loop without maintaining stateful message attributes on the central engine.

XCV: PRUNING KEYBOARD ENTITY FROM INGESTION AND VALIDATION PIPELINES
    Purpose: Remove the obsolete 'Keyboard' entity wrapper and pass the button map directly across assembly, ingestion, and validation boundaries.
    - Following the migration to 'KBService', 'Keyboard' remained only as an unnecessary data container around 'dict[str, Button]' during asset ingestion.
    Actions:
    - Removed the 'Keyboard' dataclass and its associated helper methods from 'content/app/entities.py'.
    - Updated 'RtcAssembler.assemble' in 'content/asset_ingestion/assemblers/rtc.py' to return 'dict[str, Button]' directly.
    - Updated 'IngestionServiceImpl.get_runtime_config' in 'content/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py' to handle the button dictionary directly without wrapping or unwrapping.
    - Refactored 'AssetValidator.validate' in 'content/asset_ingestion/validators/assets.py' to accept 'button_map: dict[str, Button]' and iterate over its values directly.
    Reflection: Completely eliminates the lingering legacy entity wrapper, simplifying parameter passing and aligning the ingestion pipeline directly with the domain data structures used by 'KBService'.

XCVI: CENTRALIZING TUI CONFIRMATION PROMPTS AND INSTRUCTIONS INTO PRESENTATION TIER
    Purpose: Centralize user-facing confirmation questions, template instructions, and error messages into presentation models while standardizing signature contracts across TUI services.
    - Confirmation prompt strings and required response phrases were fragmented across AppEngine and TUIServiceImpl, leaving magic strings and optional defaults in service contracts.
    Actions:
    - Introduced `UserQuestions` in `content/app/presentation.py` to hold standardized confirmation constants (`REQUIRED_PHRASE`, `INIT_REPO`, `CONFIRMATION_INSTRUCTIONS`, `CONFIRMATION_INVALID_ERR`) and dynamic prompt formatters (`overflow_proceed`, `complaints_proceed`).
    - Updated `TUIService` abstract contract in `content/app/deps/tui.py` to make `required_phrase: str` a mandatory parameter in `get_confirmation`.
    - Refactored `TUIServiceImpl.get_confirmation` in `content/tui/tui_service.py` to remove default `None` fallbacks and format instruction/error templates using `UserQuestions`.
    - Updated `AppEngine.run` and `AppEngine._bootstrap` in `content/app/engine.py` to reference `UserQuestions` members and pass `REQUIRED_PHRASE` explicitly.
    Reflection: Cleanly isolates all textual user inquiry definitions within the presentation module and enforces strict explicit parameter passing across TUI confirmation boundaries.

XCVII: REFINING WORKSPACE SETUP, TEMPLATE COPYING, AND REPO CONTRACT INITIALIZATION
    Purpose: Modernize workspace initialization by introducing explicit template constants, safe presence assertions, and direct file-to-file copying support while instantiating a root README template to align with the repository contract system vision.
    - Previous workspace initialization relied on implicit file operations and hardcoded paths without safe file-level pre-checks or generating standard root-level repository contract files like 'README.md'.
    Actions:
    - Declared `WorkspaceAlreadyInitialized` exception in `app/exceptions.py` for targeted errors when workspace directories or target files pre-exist.
    - Defined `TemplatePaths` in `app/constants.py` to centralize paths for system templates including configuration, documentation, and the new root `README.template`.
    - Extended `FileBridgePort` contract and `FileBridge` implementation (`disk_adapter.py`) with `assert_dir_absent`, `assert_file_absent`, and a unified `copy_file` adapter handling extension transformations.
    - Re-exported `FileBridge` through `content/ports_adapters/adapters.py` to maintain modular imports across domain layers.
    - Refactored `initialize_workspace` in `IngestionServiceImpl` to assert absence of both `.clanker` directory and root `README.md` before copying `config.yaml`, root `README.md`, and documentation templates via `TemplatePaths`.
    Reflection: Establishes safe, deterministic workspace creation logic with explicit path definitions while incorporating root `README.md` generation, inching the system closer to a formal repository contract standard.

XCVIII: HEADLESS TEST SYSTEM AND QUALITY GATE PIPELINE (PHASES 1 & 2)
    Purpose: Establish an automated, headless quality gate pipeline capable of running deterministic tests against isolated repository sandboxes with flexible input streams.
    - Testing clanker manually was slow, error-prone, and lacked reproducible isolated workspace fixtures.
    Actions:
    - Implemented `ScriptedTerminalAdapter` adhering to `TerminalPort` to simulate user input sequences, record UI frames/clipboards, and dump execution metrics to JSON reports.
    - Updated `clanker.py` with CLI flags (`--test`, `--input-script`, `--report-path`) to conditionally swap in `ScriptedTerminalAdapter`.
    - Created `ship_gate.py` with an OOP fixture test framework (`BaseFixtureTest`, `GateInspector`) managing sandbox setup, headless execution, and test assertion aggregation.
    - Created `empty_repo` persistent template directory and established `EmptyRepoTests` in `assert_classes.py` to assert clean program exits via `ESC` or `Ctrl+C`.
    - Shifted sandbox wipe and report cleanup to a single global execution phase at the start of `ship_gate.py`.
    - Added character stream flattening in `ScriptedTerminalAdapter` to allow mixed strings and control sequence arrays in test input definitions.
    Reflection: Provides a robust foundation for automated UI testing, enabling fast feedback loops without manual key-press cycles across various repository fixture states.

XCIX: FILESYSTEM ASSERTIONS AND REPOSITORY CONTRACT VERIFICATION (PHASE 3)
    Purpose: Enable post-execution verification of created filesystem structures and contracts within test sandboxes.
    - The quality gate required capabilities to verify that repository initialization (`clankerize`) actually generates the required filesystem layout and files.
    Actions:
    - Extended `BaseFixtureTest` in `ship_gate.py` to evaluate `fs_paths_exist` specifications against active sandboxes post-execution, supporting optional exit code / exit message keys.
    - Added `assert_clankerize_repo_contract` to `EmptyRepoTests`, dynamically evaluating presence of all paths defined in `RepoContract` following a `"yes"` confirmation sequence.
    Reflection: Completes automated verification for the workspace initialization lifecycle, allowing declarative verification of expected repository contract artifacts.

C: PORTS AND ADAPTERS REFACTORING AND ADAPTER ISOLATION (PHASE 1)
    Purpose: Clean up ports and adapters architecture by introducing domain-aligned naming conventions, isolating individual adapters into dedicated modules, and enforcing exception contracts across infrastructure boundaries.
    - Legacy ports used generic naming (`FileBridgePort`, `IOBridgePort`, `ConfigIngestorPort`), and adapters were co-located inside a monolithic `adapters.py` module.
    Actions:
    - Renamed ports in `content/ports_adapters/ports.py` to `DiskPort`, `TerminalPort`, and `ConfigParserPort`, keeping domain infrastructure exceptions (`NoSuchFile`, `FileAccessError`) adjacent to port declarations.
    - Refactored `content/ports_adapters/disk_adapter.py` by renaming `FileBridge` to `LinuxDiskAdapter` implementing `DiskPort`.
    - Created `content/ports_adapters/terminal_adapter.py` housing `LinuxTerminalAdapter` implementing `TerminalPort`.
    - Created `content/ports_adapters/yaml_parser.py` housing `RuamelYamlParserAdapter` implementing `ConfigParserPort`.
    - Removed legacy definitions from `content/ports_adapters/adapters.py`.
    - Updated initialization in `content/clanker.py` to import and instantiate the newly isolated adapters directly.
    Reflection: Establishes a clean, modular ports-and-adapters boundary where each infrastructure concern is isolated in its own adapter file adhering to strictly named port contracts.

CI: UNIFIED COMPLAINT REPORTING AND ERROR COLLECTION SIMPLIFICATION
    Purpose: Streamline error collection across asset ingestion by eliminating distinct domain overflow reporting pathways in favor of a single unified complaint reporting mechanism.
    - Maintaining a separate `DomainOverflow` dataclass and `get_domain_overflow_report` method added redundant reporting pathways and extra interface surface area.
    Actions:
    - Removed `get_domain_overflow_report` from the `Report` interface in `content/app/deps/ingestion.py`.
    - Updated `AppEngine._bootstrap` in `content/app/engine.py` to remove domain overflow confirmation checks and rely strictly on `report.get_complaints()`.
    - Cleaned up `ErrorCollector` in `content/asset_ingestion/commons/error_collector.py` by removing `_domain_overflows` state storage and domain overflow methods.
    - Removed `DomainOverflow` dataclass from `content/asset_ingestion/assemblers/rtc.py` and updated `_populate_domain_buttons` to record domain overflow warnings directly via `collector.add_complaint`.
    Reflection: Reduces interface clutter and unifies startup error reporting under a single, consistent complaint pipeline across ingestion workflows.

CII: EXCEPTION ARGUMENT HYGIENE, EXCEPTION POLICY INTEGRATION, AND ADAPTER DECOUPLING (PHASES 1-5)
    Purpose: Enforce runtime parameterless exception instantiation across the application hierarchy, integrate exception policy chaining, and completely decouple domain exceptions from the infrastructure adapter layer.
    - System exceptions previously permitted positional/keyword message arguments, and infrastructure adapters raised domain-specific exceptions directly, violating architectural boundary isolation and cluttering adapter code with business rules.
    Actions:
    - Overrode `BaseEx.__init__` in `app/exceptions.py` to reject all positional and keyword arguments, raising `IllegalExArgs` with a synthetic `ValueError` cause if violated, and updated `ExceptionPolicy` to treat all exceptions as parameterless.
    - Standardized system-wide exception raising to parameterless syntax (`raise ExName` or `raise ExName from cause`), transferring descriptive diagnostic context strictly through cause chaining.
    - Consolidated port-adjacent exceptions in `ports_adapters/ports.py` by introducing `AssetExists(Notice)` and `TerminalFailure(Fatal)`, and updated `DiskPort` to replace split absence assertions with a single `assert_absent(tokenized_path: str)` interface method while removing `get_contents_with_pud_fallback`.
    - Refactored `LinuxDiskAdapter`, `LinuxTerminalAdapter`, `ScriptedTerminalAdapter`, and `RuamelYamlParserAdapter` to eliminate all domain exception imports, raising only port-adjacent parameterless exceptions (`NoSuchFile`, `AssetExists`, `FileAccessError`, `TerminalFailure`, `ConfigParseError`).
    - Translated port-level exceptions into domain exceptions at service boundaries, updating `IngestionServiceImpl` to catch `AssetExists` and `ConfigParseError` to raise `WorkspaceAlreadyInitialized` and `ConfigAssembly` respectively.
    - Refactored `_res_multi_doc` in `RenderServiceImpl` to handle multi-doc fallback resolution, path token mapping, and duplicate file collision checks (`IllegalDuplicateFile`) in the service layer using string parsing and standard `DiskPort.get_files` calls.
    Reflection: Completely isolates infrastructure adapters from business logic, establishes a strict parameterless exception convention across all application layers, and simplifies system diagnostics through explicit `__cause__` trace chaining.

CIII: ASSET VALIDATOR SPLIT INTO FILESET AND FILELIST VALIDATORS
    Purpose: Decouple asset pool verification for file patterns from explicit filename collision detection and missing asset resolution.
    - Resolving both wildcard pattern matching and explicit file references in a single validator mixed concerns and made error context tracking fragile across repository boundaries.
    Actions:
    - Extracted `FilesetValidator` to validate pattern-based includes against PUD and Shared asset pools for `RepoContentResolver` and `ManifestResolver`.
    - Introduced `FilelistValidator` to detect repository-internal filename collisions (independent of subpath) within PUD and Shared pools.
    - Updated `FilelistValidator` to detect unbacked file references in `MultiDocResolver` across domains and base resolvers, mapping resolved paths to `PathTokens` or stripping invalid references with complaints.
    Reflection: Separates structural path pattern validation from explicit file existence and duplicate handling, clarifying error diagnostics and streamlining resolver file path mapping.

CIV: MULTI-DOC RESOLUTION SIMPLIFICATION VIA PRE-RESOLVED FILE PATHS
    Purpose: Streamline runtime multi-doc rendering by leveraging ingestion-time file path pre-resolution and reference pruning.
    - `RenderServiceImpl._res_multi_doc` previously performed redundant filesystem scans, local map assemblies, and runtime collision/existence checks that duplicated work performed during ingestion validation.
    Actions:
    - Added an optional `path: str | None = None` attribute to the `File` entity to store pre-resolved asset token paths.
    - Updated `FilelistValidator` to resolve and assign `File.path` using `PathTokens` (prioritizing PUD over Shared) and prune unbacked `File` objects directly from resolvers while issuing informative complaints.
    - Extended `FilelistValidator` to process base resolvers in parallel with domain resolvers to ensure base resolver file references are properly populated and validated.
    - Simplified `RenderServiceImpl._res_multi_doc` to read directly from `file_obj.path`, removing redundant collision detection logic, local maps, and obsolete exception handling.
    Reflection: Offloading path mapping and validity checks to the ingestion phase eliminates runtime filesystem overhead and simplifies the rendering pipeline, though handling `base_resolvers` separately in validation highlighted the need to treat base resolvers as mandatory domain includes in future refactoring.

CV: BASE RESOLVER NORMALIZATION INTO DOMAIN LISTS AND FILELIST VALIDATOR STREAMLINING
    Purpose: Streamline FilelistValidator workflows by standardizing base resolvers as mandatory pre-appended includes within all domain resolver lists.
    - Base resolvers previously bypassed the core domain structure during extraction, forcing dedicated validation paths, duplicated extraction functions, and split union handling in FilelistValidator.
    Actions:
    - Updated `DomainsExtractor.extract` to accept `base_resolvers` and prepended them to the `resolvers` list of each extracted `Domain`.
    - Simplified `IngestionServiceImpl.get_runtime_config` to pass `base_resolvers` into `DomainsExtractor.extract` and removed `base_resolvers` from the `FilelistValidator.validate` call signature.
    - Removed `_detect_unbacked_filerefs_of_base_resolvers` and `_extract_base_resolver_existencereqs` from `FilelistValidator`.
    - Restored targets in `FilelistValidator._handle_unbacked_file` exclusively to `list[Domain]`, removing `Resolver` union handling.
    Reflection: Eliminates duplicated base-resolver validation paths and type union handling by embedding base resolvers directly into the domain structure at extraction time, yielding a cleaner and more maintainable ingestion pipeline.